      "node_id": "kg_doc_1",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Graham Linehan ( ; born 22 May 1968) is an Irish television comedy writer and director who, often in partnership with Arthur Mathews, has written or co-written a number of popular television comedies. He is most noted for the sitcoms \"Father Ted\", \"Black Books\" and \"The IT Crowd\". Amongst others, he has also worked on \"Big Train\", \"Count Arthur Strong\", \"Brass Eye\" and \"The Fast Show\".",
